# Project: Portfolio Website
# Stack: React 19 + TypeScript 5 + Vite + Tailwind CSS 4

You are working on a personal portfolio site with four pages: Home, About,
Projects, Education. Follow these rules on every generation and edit.

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict mode. Never use `any`. Prefer explicit interfaces/types
  over inferred `object` shapes for props and data.
- Functional components only. No class components.
- Named exports only. No default exports.
- Tailwind CSS for all styling. No inline styles, no CSS modules, no
  styled-components.
- No TODO comments left in committed code — finish the task or flag it in
  chat, don't stub it silently.

## Architecture
- Components live in `src/components/<FeatureName>/`, one component per
  file, e.g. `src/components/Projects/ProjectCard.tsx`.
- Shared/cross-page pieces (Nav, Footer, Layout, ContactStrip) live in
  `src/components/Layout/` and `src/components/Contact/`.
- Static content data (projects, education) lives in `src/data/` as typed
  TypeScript files, not hardcoded inline in components.
- All shared types live in `src/types/index.ts`. Don't redeclare a type
  locally if an equivalent already exists there — import it.
- Routing via React Router; route definitions live in `src/App.tsx` (or
  `src/routes.tsx` if the router config grows).

## Components
- Every component takes a typed `props` interface named `<ComponentName>Props`,
  defined directly above the component in the same file.
- Keep components single-responsibility: a component that renders a list
  maps over data and delegates each item to a smaller child component
  (e.g. `ProjectGrid` maps to `ProjectCard`, not inline JSX per item).
- Responsive by default: mobile-first Tailwind classes, with `md:`/`lg:`
  breakpoints added explicitly, not assumed.
- External links (GitHub, LinkedIn, etc.) always use
  `target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"`.

## Data & Content
- Never invent placeholder personal content (bio text, project
  descriptions, credentials). If content is missing, leave the exact
  field empty or flag it in chat — don't fabricate.
- Project and education data are the single source of truth in
  `src/data/`. Components read from there, never hardcode duplicate copy.

## Before Finishing a Task
- No unused imports, variables, or props.
- No console.log left in committed code.
- Confirm the component renders correctly at mobile, tablet, and desktop
  widths before considering a task done.
